{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_310b2b3d-271a-5b46-9e0c-344d0bed741d",
  "name": "14.2 Dividing fractions and whole numbers",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dividing fractions and whole numbers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Divide a fraction by a whole number and a whole number by a fraction."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Division can mean sharing a quantity equally, or finding how many groups of a given size fit into a quantity. To divide by a nonzero number, multiply by its reciprocal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A fraction divided by a whole number k is a/b × 1/k. A whole number k divided by a fraction a/b is k × b/a. Keep the dividend unchanged and take the reciprocal of only the divisor."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockImage",
        "attrs": {
          "blockObject": {
            "block_uuid": "block_53fce4bb-578e-5aca-88d6-f6ae290222c3",
            "content": {
              "file_id": "5ac8bf91-987d-5798-8ecf-5ef27e8601be",
              "file_format": "png",
              "activity_uuid": "activity_310b2b3d-271a-5b46-9e0c-344d0bed741d"
            }
          },
          "size": {
            "width": 900
          },
          "alignment": "center",
          "unsplash_url": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_name": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_url": null,
          "unsplash_photo_url": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eight pieces of length 3/4 metre fit in a 6-metre ribbon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Share 3/5 litre equally among 4 cups."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3/5 ÷ 4 = 3/5 × 1/4 = 3/20 litre."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How many pieces of length 3/4 m can be cut from 6 m of ribbon?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = 8 pieces."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work these out in your notebook before looking at the self-check below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Find 7/8 ÷ 7."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
